RAWRXD_STUB_CENSUS_CANONICAL_001
==================================
THE LEDGER-AUTHORITY DEFECT, DECOMPOSED.

TOOL = rawrxd/tools/stub_census_canonical.ps1
HEAD AT MEASUREMENT = e7fb2efa0 "RAWRXD_DIRECT_IO_ARENA_AND_MANIFEST_001"
  (NOTE: the baseline used earlier in this work was f66d63e05. HEAD has moved
   again. The tree is not stationary, which is itself part of the finding.)


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. CANONICAL DEFINITION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
A count is admissible only alongside its RULE, its ROOT and its EXTENSION SET.
Five named rules, all implemented:

  R1_FIRSTLINE_STUB    first non-blank line matches ^//\s*STUB
                       -- THE HISTORICAL RULE. Reproduced only for comparison.
  R2_ANY_STUB          any line matches ^\s*//\s*(STUB|Auto-generated stub)
  R3_AUTO_STUB         any line matches "Auto-generated stub"
  R4_ZERO_NONCOMMENT   no ; { } ( ) = survives stripping block comments, line
                       comments and preprocessor lines.
                       -- This is the rule rawrxd_filter_missing_sources()
                          already applies in the build graph.
  R5_TRIVIAL_MAIN      body reduces to int main(){ return 0; }

  ROOT      = rawrxd_all | src_only | src_and_tests
  EXT       = EXT_NO_HEADER (.cpp .c .cc .cxx) | EXT_WITH_HEADER (+ .h .hpp)
  EXCLUDED  = build, build_*, .git, 3rdparty, out, bin, obj, node_modules, .vs
  DUPLICATES= de-duplicated by full path (two roots must not double-count)


